    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on 2026-08-17, our focus remains on maximizing volume against mediocre pitching to compensate for our ongoing roster attrition. **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) and **Andy Pages** (74.42) are our definitive offensive pillars today, both benefiting immensely from a plus-matchup against Sugano. The 4.93 xERA for Sugano represents our highest leverage point, and with **Kyle Tucker** boasting a 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and favorable park factors, he is an auto-start candidate. **Drake Baldwin** (71.19) also earns a high-tier start in the leadoff spot against Ober; his 0.373 xwOBA and the 10% order bonus effectively negate the marginal starting pitcher risk.\n\nOur internal decision-making process for the middle infield was particularly tight, with **Sam Antonacci** (42.58) narrowly holding his spot despite a significant 9% penalty for the left-on-left platoon matchup against Imanaga. While **Sam Antonacci** is technically a marginal play, we are forced to lean on him due to the unfortunate IL status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. **Gunnar Henderson** (50.62) and **Coby Mayo** (52.72) face a difficult challenge against McClanahan; while both are strictly in the \"marginal\" tier due to the SP skill and platoon resistance, we cannot afford to bench them given the lack of viable alternatives like **Josh Jung** or **Curtis Mead** on the bench today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved evaluating our depth against the volatility of today\u2019s matchups. While we considered rotating **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.59) out due to his 15% dynamic platoon penalty against Buehler, his raw speed and upside in the 5x5 Roto landscape are simply too valuable to relegate to the bench, especially with **Jacob Wilson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** unavailable. We are monitoring weather closely, but the primary risk remains the high concentration of left-handed bats\u2014including **Miguel Vargas** and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014facing southpaws. We are essentially betting on the talent of our core to outperform the negative platoon variables, as we need every point in our quest to maintain efficiency while balancing our limited remaining game caps.",
